# Paths excluded from `git archive`, i.e. from every deployment bundle built by
# deploy/aws/build_aws_bundle.sh (both the SaaS tarball and the --edition one).
#
# Why this file exists: the Edition bundle is unpacked on a paying customer's own
# server, and the customer reads it. Before this, a studio that paid for
# PWE Studio Edition received, inside their own delivery:
#
#   * docs/sales/ — the sales deck WITH the price list, and talk_track.md, which
#     is our guidance on how to answer that customer's own price objections
#   * docs/HANDOFF_*.md and docs/Project_Audit_*.md — internal engineering
#     handoffs and an open findings list (3 HIGH / 13 MED / 20 LOW)
#   * docs/design/brand/round2/ — logo research including a weighted scoring
#     table written from an imagined client's perspective
#   * .claude/ — 185 files of internal agent tooling, ~2.8 MB of dead weight
#
# None of it is referenced by any runtime, script, or deployment step (verified
# by grep over backend/, deploy/, standalone-edition/). It is internal material
# that simply travelled with `git archive HEAD`.
#
# Operator-facing docs stay in the bundle on purpose: docs/Deployment.md,
# docs/Admin_Guide.md, docs/guides/ role manuals, docs/API.md, docs/Database.md,
# deploy/aws/README_AWS.md and all of standalone-edition/ (COMMERCIAL.md
# included — those are the customer's own contract terms, which CUSTOMER_README
# links to).

# Internal agent/skill tooling.
.claude/            export-ignore
.github/             export-ignore

# Commercial material: pricing deck and objection handling.
docs/sales/         export-ignore

# Showcase seed *sources*. The demo reset reads seed-assets/showcase/ via its
# manifest.json — 30 processed assets, none of them from here. This tree is the
# unrecompressed originals kept for regeneration, and shipping it put 72 MB of
# files the server never opens into every deployment bundle.
backend/seed-assets/lets-paint-showcase-generated/ export-ignore

# Internal engineering notes and audit findings.
docs/HANDOFF_LATEST.md          export-ignore
docs/HANDOFF_2026-07-26.md      export-ignore
docs/Project_Audit_2026-07-27.md export-ignore

# Logo exploration and client-perspective scoring. The shipped brand assets and
# render_assets.py stay — they generate the product's own icons.
docs/design/brand/round2/ export-ignore

# Historical prompts/reviews are useful in Git archaeology but are not
# operator or customer documentation.
codingprompt.md                              export-ignore
docs/Current_Sprint.md                       export-ignore
docs/UX_Review_2026-07-25.md                 export-ignore
docs/Release_Readiness_2026-07-12.md         export-ignore
docs/Project_Review_Implementation_2026-07-14.md export-ignore

# The Edition installer writes these on the customer's box; never ship one.
standalone-edition/.env     export-ignore
standalone-edition/.env.bak export-ignore
